strumented binary if apps start aborting in __run_exit_handlers).\\n  ! DFTRACER_BUILD_VARIORUM=ALWAYS: an already-installed variorum is usually built for none of this machine's power domains and fails at init with _ERROR_VARIORUM_UNSUPPORTED_PLATFORM.\\n  ! rocm_path_for_variorum is the NEWEST ROCm on this node, which is not necessarily the one the app was built against. When a session has an app-matched ROCm (session_detect's features.rocm.path), that one wins — two rocm_smi ABIs in one process is the failure mode above.\\n\\n### Recommended session_detect features\\n  - `variorum` = True\\n  - `variorum_build` = ALWAYS\\n  - `rocm_path_for_variorum` = /opt/rocm-7.2.1\\n  - `papi_supported` = True\\n  - `papi_hardware_counters` = 5\\n  - `papi_events` = ['PAPI_TOT_CYC', 'PAPI_TOT_INS']\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Detected system: **corona** (from hostname `corona82`)\n\n## System: corona\n**Corona HPC system with Intel classic toolchain, MVAPICH2, and Flux wrapper launchers**\n- sudo available: False\n- MPI launcher: `flux run`\n\n### Modules (load in order)\n  1. StdEnv\n  2. intel-classic/2021.6.0-magic\n  3. mvapich2/2.3.7\n  4. flux_wrappers/0.1\n\n### Notes\nDetected from hostname corona82. Application launch scripts use flux/flux_wrappers rather than bare mpirun. Load Lmod init before module operations; use the app's own scripts as the source of truth for exact module/env setup on this system.\n## Tracing features (probed on this node)\n\n### PAPI hardware counters\n  version: 5.6.0.0  (module: `not pinned`)\n  prefix: `/usr`\n  **hardware counters: 5** — 26 presets are listed, but only this many fit at once;\n  ask for more and PAPI time-shares them and reports scaled estimates, with a zero exit code.\n  derived presets (cost >= 2 counters each): PAPI_TLB_IM, PAPI_L1_ICH, PAPI_L1_TCA\n\n  components:\n    - `perf_event` enabled — Linux perf_event CPU counters\n    - `perf_event_uncore` DISABLED — No uncore PMU