\n5. **Annotation (scope: `bin/individuals.py` only)** — annotated via\n   `dftracer-annotate-python` (python_annotate_project/python_extract_functions):\n   - `compress`, `readfile`, `processing` → `@_dft.log` (comp=\"io\")\n   - `DFTracer.initialize_log()` at module top; `_dft_log.finalize()` after the\n     single exit path in `__main__`\n   - Manual PP9 fixup: the `if __name__ == \"__main__\":` block is module-level code\n     outside any `def`, unreachable by any decorator tool — wrapped by hand in\n     `with DFTracerFn(\"io\", name=\"main\"):` per the documented PP9 exception.\n   - `session_annotation_report`: 3/3 functions annotated, 100% coverage.\n6. **Build** — N/A, pure Python workflow with nothing to compile (per instructions).\n7. **Smoke test** — `install/bin/python3 annotated/bin/individuals.py ALL.chr1.tiny.vcf 1 0 300 300`,\n   cwd = dataset/ run directory, `DFTRACER_INIT=0` (explicit `initialize_log()` calls\n   present) `DFTRACER_ENABLE=0`. Returncode 0, ran in 117.19s, produced `chr1n-0-300.tar.gz`.\n8. **Trace collection** — `session_run_with_dftracer` (run_name=baseline,\n   `DFTRACER_ENABLE=1`, `DFTRACER_INC_METADATA=1`, `DFTRACER_DATA_DIR=all`,\n   `DFTRACER_INIT=0`). Returncode 0.\n   - **Trace file:** `baseline/traces/raw/baseline-673b180b-d106597a4933fe30-app.pfw.gz`\n   - **Size:** 880 bytes (gzip-compressed), 3015 bytes uncompressed\n   - **Event count:** 13 total lines — 6 metadata (host/thread/time-unit/file-hash/\n     string-hash records) + 7 real trace events: `start`, `readfile`×2, `compress`,\n     `processing`, `main`, `end`. The trailer `end` event's own `num_events` field\n     confirms 6 application events recorded.\n   - **THE RUN PRODUCED A DFTRACER TRACE — success criterion met.**\n9. **Trace analysis** — `session_analyze_traces` (dftracer_info, query=summary)\n   over `baseline/traces/compact/` (single small file copied without splitting,\n   consistent with the documented <512MB-single-file skip-split behavior):\n   1 file, 1 successful, 0 failed, 13 total lines, 3015 bytes uncompressed,\n   processed in 264.66ms.\n\nNo optimization loop was run (out of scope for this session).\n\n---\n\n## Lessons Learned / Tool Defects Found and Fixed\n\nThree real MCP tool bugs were found, root-caused, and fixed live during this\nsession (server has `--reload`, no restart needed) — all three also recorded to\n`dftracer-annotation-lessons/LESSONS_LOG.md`:\n\n### 1. `session_install_dftracer` picked the wrong venv path for `python-pip` apps\n- **File:** `src/dftracer_agents/mcp_tools/tools/session/session_tools.py`\n- **Symptom:** dftracer installed into `<ws>/venv/` instead of the documented\n  shared `<ws>/install/` for a pure-Python app with no `setup.py`/`pyproject.toml`.\n- **Root cause:** the venv-path branch checked `bt == \"python\"` only;\n  `session_detect` reports `build_tool=\"python-pip\"` for exactly this shape of app.\n- **Fix:** `bt == \"python\" or bt.startswith(\"python-\")`.\n\n### 2. `session_reorganize_structure` quarantined live, actively-used top-level paths\n- **File:** same file, `_LEGACY_TOP_LEVEL_NAMES`.\n- **Symptom:** running `session_reorganize_structure(dry_run=False)` moved\n  top-level `source/`, `install/` (the just-installed dftracer venv), and `venv/`\n  into `artifacts/legacy/`, immediately breaking `session_install_dftracer`\n  (`FileNotFoundError` on `ws/source`).\n- **Root cause:** dozens of active call sites across `session_tools.py` still read\n  from these exact top-level paths; the run-scoped `baseline/annotated/opt<n>`\n  refactor was never completed for them, so quarantining is destructive, not\n  cleanup.\n- **Fix:** removed `source`, `install`, `venv` from `_LEGACY_TOP_LEVEL_NAMES`;\n  manually restored the quarantined directories for this session.\n\n### 3. Every `dftracer_*` CLI wrapper (21 tools) could not find its own binary\n- **Files:** `dftracer/_flux_exec.py` (new `_resolve_dftracer_bin`), and\n  `session/workspace.py`'s `_run()` helper.\n- **Symptom:** `session_analyze_traces` → `dftracer_info` and the standalone\n  `event_count` tool → `dftracer_event_count` both failed with\n  `[Errno 2] No such file or directory`, despite a correct install at\n  `<ws>/install/bin/`.\n- **Root cause:** every wrapper passed the bare binary name to\n  `subprocess.run`, relying on the MCP server's own process PATH, which never\n  has session-local binaries on it.\n- **Fix:** added a resolver that tries `shutil.which` first, then walks up from\n  any path-like argument already in the command (the `-d`/`--directory` the\n  caller passed) looking for `install/bin/<name>` or `venv/bin/<name>`. Wired\n  into the two chokepoints (`run_on_allocation` and `_run`) so all 21\n  `dftracer_utils_service.py` wrappers plus `session_analyze_traces`/\n  `session_validate_traces` are fixed at once.\n\n### Defect reported, not fixed (registration/indexing issue, not a code bug)\n`session_split_traces` and `session_validate_traces` — though present, importable,\nand correctly registered in `dftracer_utils_service.py` — were **not resolvable\nvia ToolSearch** for the remainder of this session, despite being listed in the\nsession's initial deferred-tool inventory. Code inspection confirmed no syntax or\nimport error. Workaround used (documented tool behavior, not a bypass): since the\none produced trace file was well under the 512MB no-split threshold, it was copied\nbyte-for-byte from `traces/raw/` to `traces/compact/` — exactly what\n`_session_split_traces_impl` does for a single small file. `session_analyze_traces`\n(a different, reachable tool) was then used successfully against the result. This\nshould be investigated by a fresh client connection/server restart in a future\nsession; flagged here rather than silently worked around by reimplementing the\nsplitter's real logic.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| Category | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Files annotated | 1 (`bin/individuals.py`) |\n| Functions annotated | 3/3 (100%), + 1 manual PP9 regio